      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We've determined that locally solved aim and look-at constraints do not give correct results when they are moved away from the origin of their parent - does that describe your issue here? If not, please describe the specific bug you're encountering in more detail, ideally including all the steps taken to trigger the issue and a description of expected and actual behavior. This will help us verify that we've actually addressed the issue you're referring to in your first sentence.\n\nIn terms of your feature suggestion, unfrozen axes are already applied in local space. If an axis is unticked, it means the local Euler angle for that axis in the affected transform will not be modified by the constraint component, which is consistent with how Unity constraints behave.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
