      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} My issue with it is that the freeze axis is relative to the parent. This leads to extra parent bones being required to set that orientation. Myself and others I think were hoping that solving in local space would mean that the axis would be relative to the resting orientation of the constrained object itself. Though honestly in the time that this beta has been out I cannot figure out what \"solve in local space\" is actually supposed to do (is there documentation anywhere?).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
