      "value": "@{5f30ecee654cd4491456a82f|full_name} \n\nSolving in local space means that the constraint is solved as though its sources are in the local space of the constraint's parent rather than in world space. In the case of both aim constraints and look-at constraints, this means that the constrained transform will look towards where the average weighted position of its sources would be if those sources were all in its own local space relative to its parent. As an example, if I have an aim constraint under one game object and then a single source with a local position of (1, 0, 2) under a separate sibling game object B, the aim constraint will aim towards the position (1, 0, 2) in the local space of A rather than aiming towards wherever the source actually is in world space.\n\nLocal solving is described in our beta documentation, with an illustration of how it affects rotation constraints: https://vrc-beta-docs.netlify.app/avatars/avatar-dynamics/constraints/#solve-in-local-space\n\nFrozen axes are applied after this process. If an axis is unfrozen, the local Euler angle of the constrained transform in that axis will retain its original value before the constraint ran. This allows that Euler angle to be affected by animations etc.\n\nHopefully this helps you interpret what's happening with your setup. If you still feel there's an issue, then please feel free to update this with more info, again ideally including an example with clear expected and actual behavior.\n\nWe have an internal fix going for the issue I mentioned earlier, so I'll mark this issue as Needs More Information for now.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
