  "details": "Currently unchecking any of the \"Freeze Rotation Axis\" checkboxes on an Aim constraint that is marked \"Solve In Local Space\" causes the constraint to behave incredibly strangely. It would be much more helpful if the \"Solve In Local Space\" checkbox would also make the constraint evaluate the axis in local space. Currently it just seems to flip around randomly along cardinal directions, or not move at all unless all axis are \"frozen\".\n\nAlternatively, I would accept a second checkbox added to \"Evaluate axis in local space\".",
